-- 7634 -- Wastrilith
#newmonster 7634
#copystats 1425
#spr1 "ForgottenRealms/wastrilith.tga"
#spr2 "ForgottenRealms/wastrilith2.tga"
#name "Wastrilith"
#descr "Wastriliths were mighty demons found in the aquatic environments throughout the lower planes. They were the favored minions of Dagon, as the water lords had once been obyriths themselves. Dagon gave them free reign over the Shadowsea so long as their predations didn't interfere with his agenda. 

A wastrilith innately corrupted nearby water sources simply by their presence, and water so corrupted served the wastrilith's dark ends. In Mordenkainen's work, Tome of Foes, he writes, 'The corruption left behind when a wastrilith visits the world can persist for decades. If left unchecked it can become a bridge to the Abyss.' 

Mortals who drank this water were delivered a deadly poison, while demons who drank of it found themselves restored.

Wastriliths were master summoners, preferring to call in minions over fighting directly. This mastery made them dangerous to bind and special precautions were necessary, making them a more costly summon than other demons of relative power. Never in any record were wastriliths known to freely cooperate with anyone, including each other, unless expressly serving the interests of Dagon."
